At Flix, we offer a dynamic work environment with competitive pay, strong growth opportunities, and a tech-driven approach to making travel more accessible, sustainable, and affordable. &nbsp;

This role owns the end-to-end operational performance of assigned routes and operational areas - from onboarding partners and training drivers to monitoring quality, managing projects, and driving continuous improvement across markets. You’ll act as a key operational partner, ensuring high standards, strong relationships, and seamless cross‑functional collaboration.

About the Role

• Route &amp; Partner Onboarding: Technically and operationally prepare bus partners for new route launches

• Route Management &amp; Quality Control:&nbsp; Monitor assigned routes for punctuality, safety, quality, and additional services

• Standards &amp; Optimization:&nbsp; Ensure continuous improvement of connections in line with FlixBus standards

• Driver Training &amp; Partner Support:&nbsp; Train drivers and provide ongoing technical and operational support to bus partners

• Relationship Management:&nbsp; Build and maintain strong, positive relationships with bus partners and other stakeholders

• Project &amp; Crisis Management:&nbsp; Lead complex operational projects and improvement initiatives from planning to implementation, ensuring clear ownership, stakeholder alignment and measurable results and implement action plans in crisis situations

• Reporting &amp; Cross-functional Collaboration:&nbsp; Contribute specialized knowledge to global and local projects, conduct vehicle/driver inspections, and keep all stakeholders informed on results and next steps

• Operational Ownership &amp; Delegation: Take ownership of assigned operational areas, independently manage day-to-day topics, and act as a reliable operational backup for the Senior Operations Manager

About You

• Bachelor’s degree or equivalent practical experience

• Minimum of 3 years of relevant experience&nbsp;and knowledge of bus operations, transportation processes, and partner management

• Fluent in English

• Strong analytical, problem-solving, and organizational skills

• High attention to detail and accuracy

• Ability to work independently and as a part of a team&nbsp;

We recognize that everyone carries a unique set of valuable skills and experiences. If you think you could have an impact even though you don't meet 100% of the requirements, we still encourage you to apply. We want to hear from you! &nbsp;

NB: Please submit your resume in English!

What We Offer

• Travel perks : 12 free Flix vouchers + 12 discount vouchers for friends &amp; family.&nbsp;

• Work from (M)Anywhere : Depending on your role, work from another location for up to 60 days per year.&nbsp;

• Hybrid work model : We are an office-first company, but we offer flexibility to balance work and life.&nbsp;

• Wellbeing support : Access confidential 1:1 counselling, courses, and stress management for yourself and up to four family members.&nbsp;

• Learning &amp; Development : Take advantage of language classes, training courses, and expert-led sessions to grow your skills.&nbsp;

• Mentoring Program : Connect with experienced colleagues to gain insights and accelerate your career.&nbsp;

To view more local benefits specific to each office location, please check out this link:&nbsp; Locations - Flix Career

Why Join Flix?

At Flix, you’ll find teams that rally together to overcome challenges and spark creativity. We believe in ownership culture - giving you the freedom to take initiative, make an impact, and shape your own career path.
As we continue to expand across the globe, you can make a real difference in how we work.

If you’re ready to grow and lead your journey, Flix is the place for you!&nbsp;

